  "limitations": [
    "This is a separate optional Retail-ON full reconstructed WowClient profile. The existing primary desktop matrix remains Retail-OFF and the application selected client remains 471ee42.",
    "Both native Windows jobs compile the actual optional Engine and WoW feature branches and execute one real linked RetailAssetTests CTest, plus actual executable entry, offline boundary, loopback transport and synthetic Grunt peer fixtures. They do not run normal game initialization.",
    "The successful synthetic Grunt authentication is not a compiled Esteria server, real account, version checksum, character selection, world entry or gameplay qualification.",
    "The two small diagnostic ZIPs and one original x64 complete-source ZIP were fully downloaded and independently read. ARM64 complete-source and both executable/PDB artifacts are API metadata only; their binary bytes were not downloaded or independently PE-parsed locally.",
    "The full original x64 source artifact was read with bounded streams, verified against exact Git blobs and original pinned CascLib/Xvid archive identities, then its reproducible 70 MB transport ZIP was removed. No source claim depends on a partial archive download.",
    "Both diagnostic profiles bind the identical source-inputs companion SHA256; the independently validated complete source transport was the x64 artifact only.",
    "Generated client descriptors from both actual builds independently match 215 player update fields and approved 254/25/32 limits against the pinned server header. This validates layout rather than the remaining runtime protocol.",
    "Local Retail storage tests use synthetic metadata fixtures, not actual Retail/Forever game assets. No unavailable client data, appearance catalog, map, shader or gameplay content is fabricated.",
    "The Windows x64 existing prebuilt codec is not claimed rebuild-equivalent to the preserved original upstream Xvid source. Complete original archives, source-owned adaptations and existing notices are retained separately from binaries."
  ],
